{"kind":"request","text":"Typed definitions: adopt the second spike's surface as the library core,\nwith eight helpers. Amends DX-T1 da58095a and DX-T2 aeec9280, after\n1761d819.\n\nSource: Hugh's direction of 28 October 2026. After the first spike proved\nbyte identity for two small definitions, he asked whether the typed form\npresents one coherent surface with consistent patterns and simple\nreadability, and had a second spike built to find out. He then asked for\nits results and the helpers it found to go into the implementation\nrequest. Branch spike/typed-definitions-20261028, commit f77e454a, directory\nspikes/typed-surface, REPORT.md inside. Run from the worktree root:\nnode_modules/.bin/tsc -p spikes/typed-surface/tsconfig.json and\nnode_modules/.bin/vitest run --config spikes/typed-surface/vitest.config.ts.\n\n1. What the second spike proved (observed run, 28 October 16:39 EDT; nine\n   witnesses, every one a file the repository already pins).\n\n   Witness                                              Result\n   lending compiles to examples/lending/definition.ts   exact pin\n   the live Counter (counting-commitments, b5582434)    exact pin\n   grow site, given the room's pinned digest            exact pin\n   grow room                                            equal in canonical spelling\n   change lane: 7 items, 5 acts incl. propose-manifest\n     (24 guards), 2 handlers incl. publication          equal to the pinned rows, canonical spelling\n   lending dap.application.json from the definition     equal\n   lending scenario file from a story on the judges     equal; every step judged as the file expects\n   tsc over the directory                               clean, 0.18 s\n\n   The vocabulary (spikes/typed-surface/lib.ts, 85 builders) has six\n   patterns: subjects (on, also.x, the scanned item, sender) with the same\n   verbs on each; one range form under none/some/count/sameSet and one\n   list form under each/has/distinct with a named, typed element;\n   conditions when/anyOf/ifPresent/refuse; one message shape for\n   tell/create/relate/index with result clauses as effects; handlers\n   written like acts; modules as functions of what the definition passes\n   down. Size: a definition written as data is a third to a half of its\n   size; one written with helpers (grow) is the same lines and four fifths\n   of the bytes.\n\n2. Change to DX-T1 and DX-T2: the library core is the second spike's\n   lib.ts, not the first's. The first spike's room.ts (typed per-act\n   handle, expected derivation, formFor, actsOn) stays as the client\n   handle item. Both spikes' witnesses become the library's tests, pins\n   unchanged for lending, the live Counter and the grow site.\n\n3. Canonical spelling (kernel item; file separately or under R-series).\n   The contract admits two spellings for a subject that is already\n   implied: a guard on the act's item may say of:\"on\" or not; an operand\n   may repeat the subject of its own form or not; a range may carry an\n   empty where/except or not. The kernel reads them alike. The pinned grow\n   room carries the redundant spelling in exactly 12 places (report-site,\n   set-vent, set-fan, set-heater, bind-zone-devices, hold, authorize,\n   propose-restoration, close-incident: of:\"on\" on guards whose subject is\n   the act's item) and change.json in exactly 5 (ask-rules and\n   propose-manifest tell addresses; request-check and review-verdict\n   operands repeating also.earlier). Lending, the Counter and the site\n   carry none. The library's compile normalizes to one spelling, so\n   re-expressing the grow room or the change lane changes their digests\n   unless the compiler reproduces author habit, which it should not.\n   Asked: make canonical spelling part of validateDefinition (refuse the\n   redundant spelling, or normalize before the digest), and migrate the\n   grow room and the change lane once. The grow room is deployed on\n   dap-grow; the migration is a deploy with its consequences. The\n   normalize function in lib.ts is the reference for the rule: a subject\n   is named only where it differs from the enclosing form's, and empty\n   lists are left out.\n\n4. Eight helpers, from writing the five definitions. Each sits on the same\n   data builders; none changes the model or the bytes. In priority order,\n   with what each removes.\n\n   a. Literals. equals, differs and where accept a literal or null and\n      wrap it. Removes most constant(...) and nothing from every file\n      (dozens in grow and lanes).\n   b. Copying fields to same-named slots. A typed on.take(f, \"kind\",\n      \"label\", \"minLevel\") emits one value or ref effect per name by the\n      slot's kind, and refuses a name that is not both a field and a slot.\n      commission-device has six such effects, report-zone four,\n      propose-manifest six.\n   c. Subjects declared once. by(item) adds the field\n      required(itemOf(item)) unless the author declares it (propose-\n      manifest's optional previous keeps its declaration). via takes a\n      typed sibling: also: ($) =\u003e ({ zone: by(zone), vent: via(device,\n      $.zone, \"vent\") }) instead of the string \"also.zone\".\n   d. Declared names. grants(...) and reasons(...) per definition give\n      typed references in place of the strings \"grow.configure\" and\n      \"hold-held\"; the manifest's role-coverage check moves to compile\n      time; compile emits the per-act refusal list that request e84e50e8\n      asks for, with no further authoring.\n   e. Rules beside their act. rule(name, expression) inline, hoisted by\n      compile into rules; the act carries its rule instead of pointing at\n      a map at the end of the file. The typed expression builder of\n      99c4756a follows.\n   f. Quantifiers over an item. none(hold, [\"held\"], (h) =\u003e [...]) for the\n      common case; range stays for except and for count bounds.\n   g. Items and acts by value. itemOf accepts the item object; fact\n      accepts the act when it is in the same definition. Cross-definition\n      facts stay strings.\n   h. Errors that point at the source. compile runs findings and\n      validateDefinition and reports each problem by act name and form,\n      with the offending form printed.\n\n   Keep as they are: operands stay plain data with no methods (that is\n   what makes byte identity and normalize trivial); modules stay functions\n   with explicit dependencies, not a class or a registry.\n\n5. Typed list elements. The spike types an element's members from the\n   act's record field (s.accepted, s.report are checked) and requires\n   elements(list, \"item\", \"child\") for a list that is a part of a fetched\n   fact, whose record another definition declares. The spike turns\n   noPropertyAccessFromIndexSignature and noUncheckedIndexedAccess off in\n   its own tsconfig for the untyped fallback. The package must not: type\n   every element, or require the declaration.\n\n6. Manifest and story builders (the typed form of the two files beside a\n   definition; fold into DX-T2 or file as DX-T4). package.ts derives from\n   the definition value: entry and definitions from the path, host profile\n   and capabilities, projection field types and nullability from the\n   slots, limits from many, states and act lists in sorted order,\n   connections from scope-typed references; it checks that views name\n   fields their source has and that roles cover every grant. story.ts\n   writes scenario format v1 by running the story on the real judges:\n   expected is the item ids the also rules resolve ($revision: id), every\n   step is judged as written and the story is refused when the judge\n   disagrees with the author, projection rows are read from the fold. The\n   author still gives: which slots a projection shows, view layout,\n   roles, assets, browser entry; which sources and fields a projection\n   step records; what each step should answer. This supersedes the\n   scenario harness request 736ca2bb and DX-B2 3770c687's generated-JSON\n   item, which 1761d819 6f already named.\n\n7. Two notes for the documentation. The attribute effect writes the party\n   list slot of the act's item from the attribution of the subject of; the\n   JSON reads as if of were the receiver; the typed verb is\n   on.attribute(\"authors\", also.commitment, [...]). Built but not\n   witnessed by any pinned definition in the spike: redact, every, notIn,\n   some, collect, authorsOf, settlesBy, withDefault, update, resultReason,\n   timed attention, level, capacity.\n\nCloses when DX-T1 and DX-T2 are superseded or amended to carry items 2,\n4, 5 and 6, and item 3 is filed as its own kernel request with the\nmigration named.","body":{"conditions":"closes when DX-T1 and DX-T2 are superseded or amended to carry the second spike's core, helpers, typed elements and manifest/story builders, and canonical spelling is filed as its own kernel request with the migration named","target_head":"06e4d33fe17937610891f29b5d1513b9e224edea","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}